ing coconut milk ice cream and enjoys experimenting in the kitchen, which Joanna agrees is fun.\n  - something delicious: Nate invited Joanna to try something super yummy that he made yesterday.\n  - dairy-free desserts: Nate enjoys coconut milk ice cream and shared that he also loves a creamy, dairy-free chocolate mousse, asking Joanna about her favorite dairy-free sweet treats.\n  - homemade coconut ice cream: Nate made homemade coconut ice cream and noted the sprinkles changed its color.\n  - something sweet: Joanna expressed interest in trying Nate's sweet recipe, specifically noting she is always up for something sweet.\n  - cooking show: Nate taught vegan ice cream recipes on his cooking show last Monday, which he enjoyed and used to learn new recipes. Joanna congratulated Nate and expressed interest in watching.\n  - desserts I bake: Joanna has been making all sorts of desserts (cookies, pies, cakes) that suit everyone's diets and will share more recipes with Nate soon. Nate previously made chocolate and vanilla swirl desserts and values Joanna's enjoyment.\n  - Nate: Nate congratulated Joanna on filming her movie from the road-trip script and asked about the coolest moment on set. He previously tried making coconut ice cream and had a game tournament pushed back.\n  - favorite dish: Nate taught people vegan ice cream recipes on his cooking show last Monday. Joanna asked Nate for his favorite dish from the show.\n  - dessert: Joanna shared a dessert recipe made with blueberries, coconut milk, and a gluten-free crust. Nate acknowledged it, saying it looks amazing and he will try it.\n  - dairy-free vanilla with strawberry filling and coconut cream frosting: Joanna likes the item described as dairy-free vanilla with strawberry filling and coconut cream frosting, referencing a past coconut recommendation from Nate.\n  - dairy-free: Joanna likes dairy-free desserts, especially those made with almond milk. Nate previously taught vegan ice cream recipes on his cooking show.\n  - sprinkles: Nate used sprinkles in homemade coconut ice cream, which changed the dessert's color.\n  - different flavors and toppings: Nate is looking forward to trying out different flavors and toppings for coconut milk ice cream.\n  - delicious food item: Joanna commented that a delicious food item looked appealing and asked if it was lactose-free.\n  - dairy-free chocolate mousse: Nate likes dairy-free chocolate mousse because it is super creamy and tastes like the real thing.\n  - dairy-free chocolate cake with raspberries: Joanna likes making a dairy-free chocolate cake with raspberries, describing it as moist, delicious, and perfectly sweet.\n  - almond milk: Joanna used almond milk last Friday to make a dairy-free dessert that she found delicious, as she avoids dairy.\n  - ice cream maker: Nate used an ice cream maker to make a dessert with coconut milk, vanilla extract, sugar, and salt, chilling it first before churning.\n  - raspberry: Joanna enjoys a chocolate raspberry tart with an almond flour crust, chocolate ganache, and fresh raspberries, which she notes is delicious.\n  - Nate: Nate congratulated Joanna on filming her movie from her road-trip script, asked about the coolest on-set moment, and commented that her food looked yummy with nice colors and kick.\n  - cooking: Joanna enjoys cooking and baking as creative outlets, focusing on making dairy-free desserts that are delicious and rewarding.\n  - vanilla extract: Vanilla extract was an ingredient Nate used to make ice cream, along with coconut milk, sugar, and salt.\n  - people in my vegan diet group: Nate shared homemade vegan ice cream with the people in his vegan diet group last Friday.\n</ENTITIES>\n","context_tokens":2000,"context_chars":8153,"retrieval_duration":0.13672327995300293,"response_duration":2.7925755977630615,"total_duration":2.9292988777160645,"grade":true,"grade_reasoning":"The generated answer accurately mentions 'coconut milk ice cream' and describes it as delicio