a hopes for positive feedback regarding her completed screenplay. (event_time: 2022-01-23T14:01:00Z)\n  - Joanna discussed her vision during the producer meetings (event_time: 2022-11-04T15:56:00Z)\n  - The turtles will be ready to play with Joanna after Nate bathes them. (event_time: 2022-11-09T17:54:00Z)\n  - Joanna has mixed emotions regarding the audition for the writing gig. (event_time: 2022-03-24T13:43:00Z)\n  - Joanna has never tried publishing a book before, but is considering making a book her first publication. (event_time: 2022-07-10T14:34:00Z)\n</FACTS>\n\n# These are the most relevant entities\n# ENTITY_NAME: entity summary\n<ENTITIES>\n  - major company: Joanna received a rejection letter from a major company after finishing her screenplay, which bummed her out. Nate asked if something specific happened with the company.\n  - production company: Joanna experienced a setback due to another rejection from a production company.\n  - rejection letter: Joanna received a generic rejection letter without much feedback from a major company after finishing her screenplay, which made her feel bummed out and disheartened.\n  - loss: Joanna received a rejection letter from a major company after finishing her screenplay, causing her to feel bummed out. The existing summary mentioned sadness and loss.\n  - Rejections: Joanna received rejections from a film contest, which Nate acknowledged as tough but encouraged her to keep trying.\n  - producers: Joanna pitched a script she created to producers yesterday, and they liked it, boosting her confidence. Previously, she set up meetings and finished a presentation for them last Friday.\n  - new opportunities: Joanna expressed hope that finishing her first screenplay would lead to new opportunities and positive feedback.\n  - Joanna: Joanna is filming her own movie based on her road-trip script. She finds every day on set awesome and is excited to show her vision.\n  - director: Joanna hopes a director falls in love with 