ovies: Joanna highly rates movies (9-10/10) for emotional impact. Nate suggested watching one of Joanna's movies together.\n  - audition: Joanna had an audition for a writing gig yesterday; she feels mixed emotions but is excited, and Nate wished her luck.\n  - movie: Joanna is filming her movie based on her road-trip script. She finds every day on set awesome and enjoys showing her vision, with Nate asking about the coolest moment.\n  - advice: Joanna gave advice to Nate after his game tournament was pushed back and he didn't make the finals. Nate acknowledged the advice.\n  - movie reccomendations: Joanna is willing to give movie recommendations, which Nate usually likes more than random movie choices.\n  - happiness: Joanna stated she will always remember moments that bring happiness and reminded Nate that it's important to stay happy and de-stress by doing what makes him happy.\n  - living room: Nate asked Joanna for pointers on what to get for his living room to make it comfy. Joanna responded positively, and Nate plans to try out her suggestions.\n  - activities you love: Joanna shared that writing projects are going well, describing the experience as a mix of highs and lows, and that her journal is her rock, viewing writing as a huge part of her life.\n  - third: Joanna asked Nate what made him get a 'third' after he mentioned not making it to the finals of a game tournament.\n</ENTITIES>\n","context_tokens":2011,"context_chars":8311,"retrieval_duration":0.24360251426696777,"response_duration":3.147069215774536,"total_duration":3.390671730041504,"grade":true,"grade_reasoning":"The generated answer describes Joanna's actions of continuing to work hard and pursue new opportunities after the rejection, which aligns with the essence of the gold answer.","completeness_grade":"COMPLETE","completeness_reasoning":"The context provides sufficient information to answer the question about what Joanna does after receiving a rejection from a production company. It mention