e great for cuddles and companionship.\n  - Chihuahua mixes: Audrey has two Chihuahua mixes named Precious and Pixie. She consulted an animal behaviorist due to her dogs not acting normally.\n  - breeder: Audrey got lucky finding a breeder nearby that has the dogs she wanted.\n  - Pepper: Pepper is one of Audrey's four dogs, described as a Lab mix. Audrey has four dogs: Pepper, Panda, Precious, and Pixie.\n  - tattoo parlor: Audrey went to the tattoo parlor to get more drawings added to her existing tattoo of her four dogs.\n  - it: The entity 'it' is commented on by Andrew regarding whether someone enjoys snoozing on it because it looks comfy. Previously, 'it' related to an unmentioned topic Audrey hadn't checked due to caring for puppy Pixie.\n  - tattoos: Audrey might get another tattoo when she decides to get another dog.\n  - people: Audrey makes jewelry from recycled objects, donates part of the profits to a cause, and recently took her pets to the salon where they were well-behaved.\n  - fur babies: Audrey mentioned she has 'fur babies'. Previously, Audrey got a tattoo of her four dogs, and Andrew asked if she was considering getting more.\n  - pups: Audrey took her pups to the beach over the weekend where they played in the ocean, which she found fun.\n  - Audrey's fur kids: Audrey's fur kids were taken to the pet salon, where they got groomed, looked cute, and were well-behaved in the new environment.\n  - Audrey (assistant): Audrey made an appointment with an animal behaviorist last Wednesday for her dogs who were acting abnormally and received tips to help with their problems.\n  - Audrey: Audrey took her dogs to the pet salon last Friday, noting they looked cute with shiny coats, behaved well, and were happy and safe.\n  - ocean: Audrey took her dogs to the beach over the weekend where they played in the ocean.\n  - picture: Andrew shared a picture of his dog looking happy while hiking, in response to Audrey mentioning getting tips from an animal behaviorist for her dogs.\n  - animal shelter: Audrey donates to an animal shelter as her way of helping out; Andrew's girlfriend volunteered at a pet shelter on Monday.\n  - backyard: Audrey has a new, bigger backyard at her new place where she set up a doggy play area with agility equipment and toys for the pooches.\n  - furry buddy: Andrew mentioned wanting a furry buddy to cuddle and hang with, following the adoption of a new puppy named Pixie.\n  - getaway from the city: Audrey is hoping to find a getaway from the city that is as nice as a previous one for an upcoming hike.\n  - party hats: Andrew asked Audrey if the pets enjoy wearing party hats and where she found their playdates.\n  - other pups: The dogs of Audrey love Fetch and Frisbee and enjoy running around and meeting other pups, who they could keep running with for hours.\n  - home: Audrey finds plants make a home peaceful. Andrew adopted a pup that is adjusting to its new home, where it needs time to get along with Toby.\n  - Audrey's pups: Audrey made an appointment with an animal behaviorist for her dogs due to abnormal behavior. She also joined a dog owners group to learn better care methods.\n  - bike routes: Andrew will show Audrey the best bike routes near the river area so they can get outside and soak up the scenery. Audrey looks forward to checking out the routes.\n  - garden: Audrey has a garden where flowers and vegetables grow. Her animals enjoy running around, exploring, and having a great time in the garden.\n  - pup-friendly: Andrew asked Audrey about plans for making her new place more pup-friendly after the dogs enjoyed the bigger backyard.\n  - animals: Andrew acknowledged the peaceful and joyful nature of animals, referencing potential adventures for Audrey's furry buddies.\n  - tails: Audrey organized a doggy playdate where the sight of many wagging tails brought joy to her.\n  - Audrey's dogs: Audrey took her dogs to the pet salon last Friday for grooming; they looked cute with shiny co