s has happened. Nate is excited to watch it.\n  - people: Joanna shared how rewarding it was to see her written work performed, drawing inspiration from real life and imagination to create characters.\n  - stories: Joanna finds happiness and fulfillment in creating stories and watching them come alive, calling writing a blessing for her.\n  - dialogue: Joanna found it rewarding to see the dialogue she wrote acted out, noting it was the third time this happened. Seeing characters and dialogue from her writing performed was an amazing experience.\n  - love story: Joanna is writing a movie script for a love story that involves many challenges; she is working hard and hopes to see it on the big screen.\n  - film festivals: Joanna submitted her screenplay to a film festival, feeling relief, excitement, and worry while hoping a producer or director selects it for the big screen.\n  - an idea: Joanna got ideas for characters from people she knows, things she saw, and her imagination, seeing them take shape with wants and worries.\n  - producer: Joanna hopes a producer or director will like her screenplay enough for it to be shown on the big screen.\n  - Joanna: Joanna is filming her own movie based on her road-trip script. She finds every day on set awesome and is excited to show her vision.\n  - movie: Joanna is filming her movie based on her road-trip script. She finds every day on set awesome and enjoys showing her vision, with Nate asking about the coolest moment.\n  - awesome characters: Joanna writes about \"wild worlds with awesome characters\" and is now in a writers group, feeling motivated by inspirational people.\n  - director: Joanna hopes a director falls in love with her screenplay to get it on the big screen.\n  - screenplay: Joanna wrote parts of a screenplay that appeared on the big screen yesterday and submitted a recent screenplay to a film contest.\n  - movie script: Joanna is filming a movie based on her road-trip script. She previously hoped for big-screen distribution, and Nate asked about future script submissions.\n  - acting: Joanna enjoys acting, especially dramas and emotionally-driven films, and might try it if given the opportunity while currently focusing on her writers group.\n  - movie: Joanna is filming her movie based on her road-trip script, finding every day on set awesome and full of potential while showing her vision.\n  - watching movies: Joanna enjoys watching movies as a hobby, in addition to writing, reading, and exploring nature.\n  - actors: Joanna watched a classic movie that had a gripping story and great actors.\n  - feelings: Writing is a way for Joanna to express her feelings, act as an escape, put thoughts down, and create something good from them, as words have a magical way of healing.\n  - dialogues exploring loss, redemption, and forgiveness: Joanna mentioned a page with dialogues exploring loss, redemption, and forgiveness for her next movie; she finds the story deep and emotional.\n  - that movie: Joanna watched 'that movie' about 3 years ago and acquired a physical copy.\n  - moods: Joanna is finding comfort and creativity by tinkering with recipes when in certain moods, which Nate finds satisfying.\n  - activities you love: Joanna shared that writing projects are going well, describing the experience as a mix of highs and lows, and that her journal is her rock, viewing writing as a huge part of her life.\n</ENTITIES>\n","context_tokens":2103,"context_chars":8712,"retrieval_duration":0.2316124439239502,"response_duration":2.2807905673980713,"total_duration":2.5124030113220215,"grade":true,"grade_reasoning":"The generated answer captures the essence of Joanna's feelings about seeing her characters come alive, using synonyms like 'amazing' and 'rewarding' which align with 'surreal and cool'.","completeness_grade":"COMPLETE","completeness_reasoning":"The context provides sufficient information to answer the question about Joanna's feelings on October 25, 2022, regarding her chara