e faith and patience because he feels his efforts at work are going unseen, despite Calvin's encouragement.\n  - fulfillment: Calvin found fulfillment visiting Boston's architecture and history. Dave finds fulfillment in his car project, as both discovered things that bring them fulfillment.\n  - Cal: Calvin (Cal) works with new talent, making a beat for a young artist with great music potential. He enjoys seeing his old friends who support him.\n  - journey: Calvin is on a musical journey, confirmed by Dave who congratulated him on a gala attendance and upcoming performance. Dave is keen to hear about it and see a show in Boston.\n  - Dave: Dave complimented Calvin's performance picture. He mentioned that Calvin's support for others keeps music going and passes on a legacy.\n  - life: Calvin is currently touring with Frank Ocean; Dave asked how he is juggling his job and personal life, referencing a prior chat about fame's impact.\n  - encouragement: Dave appreciated Calvin's encouragement after a tough week where a deal was lost, believing patience will lead to positive outcomes.\n  - the sea: Calvin's Japanese artist friend made an item featuring an octopus, representing Calvin's love for art and the sea.\n  - mark: Calvin mentioned that every 'mark' and strum holds a story when discussing his performance on a big stage.\n  - California Love: Dave mentioned to Calvin that \"California Love\" is a classic song and suggested jamming to music together.\n  - strum: Calvin mentioned that every 'mark and strum holds a story' about his performance on a big stage.\n  - loved ones: Calvin's family and friends, referred to as loved ones, attended a party at his Japanese house celebrating his new album release.\n  - garage: Dave's garage is a little dirty but everything is in place; it's where he tinkers with cars, an activity he finds calming. Calvin looks forward to seeing it.\n  - mutual friend: Calvin's mutual friend arranged a meeting for Calvin with incredible artists