ut plans for making her new place more pup-friendly after the dogs enjoyed the bigger backyard.\n  - ways to relax: Audrey mentioned organizing a doggy playdate with neighbors' dogs as a way to relax and find joy.\n  - dogs: Audrey took her dogs to the pet salon; they looked cute, groomed, and had shiny coats. Andrew has two dogs, Toby and Buddy. They are considered family members.\n  - the doggos: Audrey takes the doggos for walks in the park to relax and clear her mind, as they offer a nature environment.\n  - puppies and dogs: Audrey has four doggies that she takes care of to keep them happy and healthy. Andrew mentioned he would not want puppies and dogs to be punished.\n  - job: Andrew finds it harder to find peace through nature due to his job and current living situation, creating a void in his heart.\n  - pets: Audrey bought dog toys last Monday. Andrew recently adopted a new puppy who is adjusting to his new home and getting along with Toby. Both find joy in pets.\n  - pet shelter: Andrew recently adopted another dog from a shelter. Previously, Andrew and his girlfriend volunteered at a pet shelter on Monday, which Andrew found rewarding.\n  - plants: Andrew mentioned getting more plants for his house; Audrey suggested plants can make a home peaceful.\n  - Andrew (assistant): Andrew asked Audrey about the tips she received from her dogs' appointment with an animal behaviorist. Andrew suggested visiting a lake near a trail to see the autumn colors.\n  - puppy: Andrew adopted a new puppy named Toby. Andrew shared photos of his puppy playing in the park, which made Andrew and Audrey happy.\n  - Andrew's girlfriend: Andrew's girlfriend creates a safe and fun space for Scout, and she is encouraged to slowly introduce Scout to Toby and Buddy.\n  - picture: Andrew shared a picture of his dog looking happy while hiking, in response to Audrey mentioning getting tips from an animal behaviorist for her dogs.\n  - Monday: On Monday, Andrew and his girlfriend volunteere