 to the pet salon; they looked cute, groomed, and had shiny coats. Andrew has two dogs, Toby and Buddy. They are considered family members.\n  - pets: Audrey bought dog toys last Monday. Andrew recently adopted a new puppy who is adjusting to his new home and getting along with Toby. Both find joy in pets.\n  - Andrew: Andrew reacted positively to Audrey's groomed pets and is preparing a space for Scout, including a bed, toys, and puppy pads, for a slow introduction to Toby and Buddy.\n  - animals: Andrew acknowledged the peaceful and joyful nature of animals, referencing potential adventures for Audrey's furry buddies.\n  - puppy: Andrew adopted a new puppy named Toby. Andrew shared photos of his puppy playing in the park, which made Andrew and Audrey happy.\n  - meadow: Andrew commented that dogs in a picture shared by Audrey look content, noting the meadow in the photo looks nice and brings joy to the pets.\n  - joy: Audrey says pets bring much joy. Andrew agrees, mentioning that the pictured pets snuggled up bring joy and fun.\n  - family: Audrey is grateful for her pets, considering them family members, while Andrew also values dogs as amazing furry friends who are always there for them.\n  - pics: Andrew asked Audrey for pictures of her groomed pets after they visited the pet salon.\n  - Scout: Andrew feels lucky to have Scout, one of his furry friends. Audrey previously suggested slowly introducing Scout to Toby and Buddy.\n  - Andrew's pup: Andrew's pup is a German Shepherd known for loyalty and smarts. Andrew is going camping with his girlfriend, Toby, and the pup.\n  - fur babies: Audrey mentioned she has 'fur babies'. Previously, Audrey got a tattoo of her four dogs, and Andrew asked if she was considering getting more.\n  - puppies and dogs: Audrey has four doggies that she takes care of to keep them happy and healthy. Andrew mentioned he would not want puppies and dogs to be punished.\n  - cuatro perros: Audrey has cuatro perros (four dogs) whom she lov