ved well.\n  - pet store: Audrey went to a pet store last Monday to buy toys for her dogs.\n  - dog-friendly place: Audrey made goodies to thank neighbors for their pup-friendly homes. Previously, Audrey encouraged Andrew to find a great dog-friendly place to live.\n  - local pet store: Audrey saw a flyer for a positive reinforcement training workshop at her local pet store.\n  - doggo: Audrey groomed her dogs, who looked cute with shiny coats after being good at the salon. Andrew adopted another dog and shared a photo.\n  - doggie playdate: Audrey recently organized a doggy playdate with neighbors' dogs, noting the sweet sight of wagging tails, which followed a previous playdate last Friday with her three 3-year-old dogs.\n  - animals: Andrew acknowledged the peaceful and joyful nature of animals, referencing potential adventures for Audrey's furry buddies.\n  - fur babies: Audrey mentioned she has 'fur babies'. Previously, Audrey got a tattoo of her four dogs, and Andrew asked if she was considering getting more.\n  - dog owners group: Audrey joined a dog owners group recently to learn better care for her four dogs and meets with the group weekly for tips and to let the dogs play together.\n  - neighbors' dogs: Audrey organized a doggy playdate with the neighbors' dogs, and seeing them wag their tails was sweet.\n  - pets: Audrey bought dog toys last Monday. Andrew recently adopted a new puppy who is adjusting to his new home and getting along with Toby. Both find joy in pets.\n  - Audrey's fur kids: Audrey's fur kids were taken to the pet salon, where they got groomed, looked cute, and were well-behaved in the new environment.\n  - Audrey's pups: Audrey made an appointment with an animal behaviorist for her dogs due to abnormal behavior. She also joined a dog owners group to learn better care methods.\n  - puppies and dogs: Audrey has four doggies that she takes care of to keep them happy and healthy. Andrew mentioned he would not want puppies and dogs to be puni