r feel bummed out and disheartened.\n  - new opportunities: Joanna expressed hope that finishing her first screenplay would lead to new opportunities and positive feedback.\n  - seeing all of the characters and dialogue I wrote being acted out: Joanna experienced seeing all of the characters and dialogue she wrote being acted out, which was rewarding and the third time this has happened to her.\n  - new things: Joanna submitted a screenplay to a film contest and mentioned that people love it when she makes them new things.\n  - feelings: Writing is a way for Joanna to express her feelings, act as an escape, put thoughts down, and create something good from them, as words have a magical way of healing.\n  - script: Joanna is filming a movie from her road-trip script. An actor praised the script, making Joanna excited and giving her chills.\n  - writing projects: Joanna is busy with writing projects, which she finds to be the best thing ever, a mix of highs and lows. Writing is an escape, a way to express feelings, and healing.\n  - screenplay: Joanna wrote parts of a screenplay that appeared on the big screen yesterday and submitted a recent screenplay to a film contest.\n  - audition: Joanna had an audition for a writing gig yesterday; she feels mixed emotions but is excited, and Nate wished her luck.\n  - producer: Joanna hopes a producer or director will like her screenplay enough for it to be shown on the big screen.\n  - Joanna: Joanna is filming her own movie based on her road-trip script. She finds every day on set awesome and is excited to show her vision.\n  - romance: Joanna's first full screenplay, finished last Friday, is a mix of drama and romance.\n  - director: Joanna hopes a director falls in love with her screenplay to get it on the big screen.\n  - writing: Joanna feels she cannot stop writing recently, appreciating Nate's support and encouragement.\n  - dialogues exploring loss, redemption, and forgiveness: Joanna mentioned a page with dialogues exploring loss, redemption, and forgiveness for her next movie; she finds the story deep and emotional.\n  - activities you love: Joanna shared that writing projects are going well, describing the experience as a mix of highs and lows, and that her journal is her rock, viewing writing as a huge part of her life.\n  - happiness: Joanna stated she will always remember moments that bring happiness and reminded Nate that it's important to stay happy and de-stress by doing what makes him happy.\n  - romantic drama: Joanna mentioned a romantic drama about memory and relationships that she found to be very good.\n  - movie script: Joanna is filming a movie based on her road-trip script. She previously hoped for big-screen distribution, and Nate asked about future script submissions.\n  - acting: Joanna enjoys acting, especially dramas and emotionally-driven films, and might try it if given the opportunity while currently focusing on her writers group.\n  - Writing and creative projects: Joanna is busy with writing projects, which she finds to be a mix of highs and lows. Her journal is a major source of support for her writing endeavors.\n  - awesome characters: Joanna writes about \"wild worlds with awesome characters\" and is now in a writers group, feeling motivated by inspirational people.\n  - memory and relationships: Joanna mentioned a romantic drama about memory and relationships that she found to be very good.\n  - movie: Joanna is filming her movie based on her road-trip script. She finds every day on set awesome and enjoys showing her vision, with Nate asking about the coolest moment.\n  - moods: Joanna is finding comfort and creativity by tinkering with recipes when in certain moods, which Nate finds satisfying.\n  - personal experiences and feelings: Joanna shared that meaningful stories arise from vulnerability, exploring personal experiences and feelings, and remaining true to oneself, as acknowledged by Nate.\n</ENTITIES>\n","context_tokens":2006,"context_char