ey takes the doggos for walks in the park to relax and clear her mind, as they offer a nature environment.\n  - walk: Andrew enjoys walks with Buddy for quality time and fresh air. Audrey mentioned her dogs enjoy walks, though she has not walked them recently.\n  - outdoors: Audrey misses taking her dogs for walks in nature, calling those moments with her pets in the outdoors chill and happy.\n  - exercise: Audrey pets and hugs her dog often for exercise and bonding. Audrey's dog, Precious, was scared, and Audrey calmed her by petting, hugging, and walking slowly.\n  - neighborhoods: Audrey's childhood memories include taking long walks with her dog, Max, in the neighborhood, where she shared worries and hopes with him.\n  - dog owners group: Audrey joined a dog owners group recently to learn better care for her four dogs and meets with the group weekly for tips and to let the dogs play together.\n  - dog owners: Audrey meets with a dog owners group once a week for tips and playdates. She considered a positive reinforcement training class workshop advertised at her pet store.\n  - city dogs: Audrey's city dogs love trying new parks and trails and go on adventures very often.\n  - pet salon: Audrey took her four dogs to the pet salon last Friday for grooming; the dogs were excited, looked cute, and behaved well.\n  - there: Audrey mentioned she'd love to take her dogs to 'there' sometime, following an appointment with an animal behaviorist.\n  - fun outings: Audrey mentioned her dogs had a blast on a road trip to a national park last Friday, enjoying walks near her home park.\n  - dog: Audrey took her four dogs to the pet salon for grooming. Andrew adopted another dog recently, managing with two dogs currently, and asked Audrey for multi-dog owner tips.\n  - hiking spots: Audrey hopes to take her dogs hiking soon and is looking for a spot with a great view and room for them to explore. Andrew hopes to find a hiking spot soon.\n  - gorgeous spot: Audrey inquired about